# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# /contracts/.env.example
#
# Copy this file to /contracts/.env and fill in the blanks. The .env file is
# gitignored at the repo root — it must NEVER be committed. This .env.example
# IS committed; it documents which variables are expected and provides safe
# default values for public facts (RPC URL, canonical contract addresses).
#
# Usage:
#   cd contracts
#   cp .env.example .env
#   $EDITOR .env       # set PRIVATE_KEY, leave the rest as-is for now
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Wallet ---
# Hex private key for the wallet that deploys contracts and runs scripts.
# Format: with or without leading 0x.
# USE A FRESH TESTNET-ONLY KEY. Never put a key holding real funds in a .env.
PRIVATE_KEY=

# --- Arc testnet RPC ---
# Primary HTTP RPC for Arc testnet (chain ID 5042002).
# Alternates: rpc.blockdaemon.testnet.arc.network, rpc.drpc.testnet.arc.network,
# rpc.quicknode.testnet.arc.network. See docs.arc.io/arc/references/connect-to-arc
ARC_RPC_URL=https://rpc.testnet.arc.network

# --- Canonical Arc testnet contracts ---
# USDC: native gas token AND the ERC-20 we pay bounties in. The very-short
# address is intentional — it's a precompile-style ERC-20 wrapper over the
# native USDC balance, exposing standard transfer/approve/transferFrom.
USDC_ADDRESS=0x3600000000000000000000000000000000000000

# ERC-8004 IdentityRegistry: ERC-721 NFT registry where agents register and
# get an agentId (= NFT tokenId). JobEscrow will call ownerOf(agentId) to
# authorize submissions, so this contract is load-bearing for v1.
IDENTITY_REGISTRY_ADDRESS=0x8004A818BFB912233c491871b3d84c89A494BD9e
